# InstitutionalEdge — End-to-End Implementation Plan

## Overview

Transform the current MVP (20 stocks, basic FII/DII accumulation score) into a **full institutional money tracking and stock selection system** — all in JavaScript (MERN stack). The system tracks where big money is moving **before it shows up in price**, scores stocks on multiple weighted factors, generates precise entry/target/SL levels, and tracks selected positions daily.

**Existing stack:**
- Backend: Node.js + Express + MongoDB Atlas + Redis (Docker)
- Frontend: Next.js 14 (TypeScript)
- Collectors: NSE FII/DII (stock-level), NSE Bulk Deals
- Analyzer: [accumulationAnalyzer.js](file:///c:/Stock-Trading/backend/src/services/accumulationAnalyzer.js) (FII + Bulk score, 2 components)

---

## Phase 1: Data Foundation

> [!IMPORTANT]
> All data comes from NSE public APIs and broker APIs — no illegal scraping. NSE uses cookie-based sessions; existing [base.js](file:///c:/Stock-Trading/backend/src/collectors/base.js) collector already handles this.

### Backend — New MongoDB Models

#### [MODIFY] [Stock.js](file:///c:/Stock-Trading/backend/src/models/Stock.js)
Add: `marketCap`, `lotSize`, `sectorIndex` (e.g. `NIFTY_BANK`) fields.

#### [NEW] OiData.js
